# MITS Altair 88-DCDD CP/M payload, packed as 32 128-byte sectors per track.
# The project's install helper converts its 137-byte physical sectors to and
# from this representation before invoking cpmtools.
# The packed image starts with one blank padding track, so the disk's 77
# tracks (2 boot) are packed tracks 1-77 and the filesystem is unchanged
# (150 2 KB blocks). libdsk-based cpmtools builds treat an odd track count
# above 43 as double-sided and drop the last track (77 -> 38 x 2), which made
# block 148 unreadable and silently unwritable.
diskdef altair88
  seclen 128
  tracks 78
  sectrk 32
  blocksize 2048
  maxdir 64
  boottrk 3
  skewtab 0,8,16,24,2,10,18,26,4,12,20,28,6,14,22,30,1,9,17,25,3,11,19,27,5,13,21,29,7,15,23,31
  logicalextents 1
  os 2.2
end